WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.740
CIBC shares sit 7% below the 170-50 fair value mark after a $1 billion note sale. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 207. After the close, we screen Canadian AI names. Walk a simulated 5-session bank hold, review Oritsia, then options flow tools, the open book, and a covered call you can run in a TFSA. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:35.880
with no real money. I'm not a license financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.205
your own research before putting real money to work. Economists are lifting the odds of a bank

00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:46.765
of Canada hike as inflation stays stubborn, and that is the macro sitting on every Canadian bank

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:55.765
name tonight. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,713, up 3 tenths of a percent, while the NASDAQ composite finished

00:00:55.765 --> 00:01:06.025
at 26,425, flat on the session. That NASDAQ print is up 13.73% year-to-date, and up 18.10%

00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:14.005
since this practice record began on March 16, 2026. The TSX composite closed at 36,108,

00:01:14.505 --> 00:01:19.505
up half a percent, with financials leading the tape and energy lagging even as oil moved

00:01:19.505 --> 00:01:25.125
higher. Markets still price a hold from the Bank of Canada on October 29, and from the

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:30.325
Federal Reserve later in the year, so the Hike Talk is a change in odds, not a decision

00:01:30.325 --> 00:01:31.245
already in the bag.

00:01:31.745 --> 00:01:37.925
About 14 days ago, we simulated AMD on a Samsung Semiconductor Partnership catalyst, and

00:01:37.925 --> 00:01:44.025
that name closed down 4.61%, which is why I am slower to size a catalyst until the sector

00:01:44.025 --> 00:01:44.685
tape agrees.

00:01:45.813 --> 00:01:50.633
Thematic investing in Canadian AI names paid when investors screened for companies already

00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:55.893
posting revenue growth above 30% and trading at reasonable multiples to that growth.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:01.493
The method is simple, find sector leadership in an emerging theme, then confirm those

00:02:01.493 --> 00:02:06.153
names have already beaten the TSX by a wide margin before you add a dollar of exposure.

00:02:06.773 --> 00:02:13.653
Two Canadian AI holdings have locked in gains of 78% and 71%, while the broader index lagged,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:18.373
which is the edge for identifying the theme early rather than chasing it once it is obvious.

00:02:19.093 --> 00:02:24.873
Implementation starts with a screen on Investing.com, Canada, or your broker's sector ETF list

00:02:24.873 --> 00:02:30.293
for AI or software holdings, then a cross-check of year-to-date performance and revenue growth

00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:31.533
from the latest filings.

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:36.993
Historically, this has worked best in the first 18 to 24 months of a new technology cycle,

00:02:37.433 --> 00:02:40.853
when earnings visibility is still expanding rather than rolling over.

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:46.653
Prior tech cycles show that names beating the TSX by more than 50% in the first year

00:02:46.653 --> 00:02:53.013
of a theme, often keep outperforming for another 12 months if revenue growth stays above 25%.

00:02:53.013 --> 00:02:54.313
The risks are real.

00:02:54.913 --> 00:02:59.693
The theme can rotate out quickly once growth rates peak, or when broader market volatility

00:02:59.693 --> 00:03:02.813
rises and high multiple software is the first thing sold.

00:03:03.473 --> 00:03:09.293
One practical step is to put no more than 5% of a tax-free savings account, or TFSA,

00:03:09.553 --> 00:03:14.393
into any single thematic name, and rebalance quarterly with the same revenue growth and

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.753
relative performance filters.

00:03:15.753 --> 00:03:20.733
on wealth, simple, or quest trade, and I have no financial relationship with either.

00:03:21.213 --> 00:03:25.933
You can build a custom watch list that flags software and semiconductor names whose 20-day

00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:29.253
average volume sits above their 50-day average before you enter.

00:03:29.993 --> 00:03:34.473
That volume filter is how those two stand out Canadian AI holdings separated themselves

00:03:34.473 --> 00:03:36.013
on the initial breakout days.

00:03:36.653 --> 00:03:38.953
Weaker names that later faded never cleared it.

00:03:38.953 --> 00:03:45.728
Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce, ticker CM on the TSX, is the simulated weekly hold,

00:03:46.208 --> 00:03:51.208
and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money attached. The entry

00:03:51.208 --> 00:03:57.388
is $159 Canadian dollars and $12 cents. A valuation gap against the consensus mark we opened

00:03:57.388 --> 00:04:03.308
on, with 20-day average volume still supportive on the recent advance. Two factors carry this,

00:04:03.308 --> 00:04:10.848
the under-valuation screen and a common equity tier 1 ratio of 13.4%, plus a 26% year-to-date

00:04:10.848 --> 00:04:16.936
share price gain that says momentum has not rolled over. Yahoo Finance also shows active share

00:04:16.936 --> 00:04:22.496
repurchase programs covering up to 3% of shares, which can support earnings per share even if

00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:30.316
loan growth slows, and a 3-year total shareholder return of 273.21%. The long-dated notes do

00:04:30.316 --> 00:04:36.096
2086 sit as fixed-to-floating paper, so the coupon can adjust if rates move, which is

00:04:36.096 --> 00:04:42.560
why the capital raise did not automatically kill the valuation case. Target is plus 4-7%

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:48.340
over 5 sessions if that valuation gap narrows. The stop sits at the 50-day moving average

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:55.020
near $152 Canadian dollars. Confidence is medium, two factors aligned, but sector rotation

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.760
into banks is not yet confirmed by volume, and I am not going to pretend the leadership

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.320
print on the TSX is the same thing as a volume confirmation.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:08.940
Eritzia just paid us for respecting catalysts and still left size on the table because

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.220
consumer discretionary rotation was never confirmed first.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:17.440
That is why this bank entry stays medium and does not get a full-size allocation until

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.640
the volume filter clears.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.320
In validation is the habit to copy.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.420
The most followed fair value estimate falls below the current share price.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.600
If that data point moves, the thesis is done, no debating, no averaging down.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.940
Primary risk remains a deeper housing slowdown or higher for longer rates, pressuring loan

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:36.440
growth.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.680
We hold five sessions from entry and evaluate on Friday unless that invalidation or the

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.360
moving average stop hits first.

00:05:44.384 --> 00:05:51.244
Eritzia, ticker ATZ on the TSX, was the last weekly hold, evaluation entry after an earnings

00:05:51.244 --> 00:05:52.604
beat and a guidance lift.

00:05:52.604 --> 00:05:59.304
We simulated buying at $143 Canadian dollars and 36 cents on the Tuesday open and exited

00:05:59.304 --> 00:06:05.024
at $150 Canadian dollars and 38 cents on the Monday close, a six calendar day window.

00:06:05.544 --> 00:06:12.344
That is a gain of 4.90% or $48.97 on a $1,000 simulated position.

00:06:12.984 --> 00:06:19.724
Over the same window, the NASDAQ gained roughly 1.8%, so the trade produced 3.1% of alpha,

00:06:19.724 --> 00:06:22.884
A win against the benchmark, not just a green number.

00:06:23.564 --> 00:06:25.004
The earnings catalyst did the work.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:29.404
The gain would have been larger if sector rotation into consumer discretionary had been

00:06:29.404 --> 00:06:31.024
confirmed before we sized it.

00:06:31.664 --> 00:06:31.824
Rule.

00:06:32.404 --> 00:06:36.904
Cross-check sector rotation signals before sizing earnings driven entries and retail names.

00:06:37.959 --> 00:06:42.939
Unusual Wales is a real-time options flow feed that surfaces large trades before the move

00:06:42.939 --> 00:06:47.219
shows up in the share price, and I have no financial relationship with the platform.

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:53.039
Canadian investors can use the free tier to monitor TSX names and the paid tier for

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:57.939
deeper filters and alerts, which is most useful if you already have a short list rather than

00:06:57.939 --> 00:07:03.159
hunting the whole market. Set alerts for Flow exceeding 500 contracts on a single strike.

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:09.139
That size often precedes headline moves in high beta names. The feed also flags unusual

00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:14.339
whale activity in names such as Tesla and SpaceX when merger-related committees form,

00:07:14.339 --> 00:07:20.479
firm, which is early visibility into a volatility spike, not a buy signal by itself. Alerts can

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:26.279
push into wealth-simple or interactive brokers watchlists, through broker APIs, so you are

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:32.082
not sitting on the feed all day. Endbridge is the income math homework. The full walks

00:07:32.082 --> 00:07:37.022
how many shares you would need at the current price to earn $1,000 of dividend income each

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:42.582
year, then asks you to compare the payout ratio with peers. Pipeline volumes recovering

00:07:42.582 --> 00:07:47.802
and possible future payout growth, make that position-size calculation especially relevant

00:07:47.802 --> 00:07:51.722
for TFSA holders who already treat the name as a yield anchor.

