CBC describes the Canadian housing market as on its knees, with stubborn inflation pushing

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:02.110
some economists to price a possible rate hike next week for the first time since the

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.910
Bank of Canada last raised in July 2023.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:10.970
An 8th consecutive hold is still widely predicted, but the action is to review any variable

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.950
rate debt you carry and model the cash flow hit of a 25 basis point increase before

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.030
that decision lands.

00:08:17.975 --> 00:08:22.795
Error's capital, the business development company, trades below net asset value with a

00:08:22.795 --> 00:08:27.095
high yield attached, and the fool's read is to wait for the upcoming earnings report

00:08:27.095 --> 00:08:28.875
rather than buy the discount blind.

00:08:29.495 --> 00:08:33.755
Compare that discount with the five-year average and let credit quality trends on the print

00:08:33.755 --> 00:08:36.275
tell you whether the gap compresses or widens.

00:08:36.275 --> 00:08:42.815
The simulated book runs $1,000 per trade under rules published on August 18th, 2026.

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:49.895
Fixed five session holds, entry at the next open, stop or horizon exits, and no discretionary

00:08:49.895 --> 00:08:50.595
early sales.

00:08:51.115 --> 00:08:52.375
Those rules are the product.

00:08:52.875 --> 00:08:56.915
You should be able to take the pick, the date, and the stop and reproduce every number

00:08:56.915 --> 00:08:57.555
