Across 84 total simulated trades, the win rate is 52%. 44 wins, 39 losses, one break even,

00:09:25.135 --> 00:09:32.815
with cumulative P&amp;L of minus $27.15, an average return of minus 0.03%.

00:09:33.075 --> 00:09:41.355
a best trade of plus 20.11%, a worst of minus 27.14%, and a current streak of four wins.

00:09:41.995 --> 00:09:50.035
Year-to-date, the simulated book is minus 0.03% against the NASDAQ composite at plus 13.73%.

00:09:50.035 --> 00:09:54.635
That buy-and-hold gap is why we measure matched windows instead of just the calendar.

00:09:55.275 --> 00:10:02.775
Open positions are ENB on the TSX, BN on the TSX, and GM, none of which overlap with today's

00:10:02.775 --> 00:10:09.067
financial sector valuation entry. You already own 100 shares of CIBC and you want extra cash

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:15.887
without selling the position. Sell a 30-day call struck at $170 for a premium of $1.80.

00:10:16.847 --> 00:10:23.907
Collected immediately, which lowers the effective cost basis to $157.20 and caps the upside

00:10:23.907 --> 00:10:29.307
if shares rally through that strike by expiry. The buyer pays you for the right to take those shares

00:10:29.307 --> 00:10:34.687
at the strike. If the stock stays below it, you keep the shares and the premium. Think of it as

00:10:34.687 --> 00:10:39.927
renting out a parking spot on land you still own. A pro habit is to read open interest and the

00:10:39.927 --> 00:10:45.367
bid asks spread on the chain before you send the order. Because a widespread on a low volume strike

00:10:45.367 --> 00:10:50.767
can erase most of the income edge. Covered calls are not free money. They reduce but do not

00:10:50.767 --> 00:10:56.667
eliminate losses if the stock falls hard. And they clip you in a strong rally. Size so the premium

00:10:56.667 --> 00:11:02.807
offsets no more than 2-3% of potential downside before you would sell the shares anyway. Inside

00:11:02.807 --> 00:11:09.247
a TFSA, or a registered retirement savings plan, or RRSP, the premium does not trigger

00:11:09.247 --> 00:11:14.387
an immediate tax bill, which is why this is a Canadian account mechanic rather than a taxable

00:11:14.387 --> 00:11:21.427
account afterthought. Delta on that 170 call typically sits around 0.25, so the position

00:11:21.427 --> 00:11:27.147
behaves like 75 shares of long stock, plus 25 shares of short stock for risk purposes.

00:11:27.707 --> 00:11:32.887
Time decay works for the seller, roughly two-thirds of the premium erodes in the final two weeks

00:11:32.887 --> 00:11:40.627
if the shares stay range-bound. A protective put struck at $150 for $2.50, paired with that call,

00:11:41.187 --> 00:11:47.747
builds a collar that floors you near $147.50 and still caps the upside at the short strike.

00:11:47.747 --> 00:11:52.667
covered structures require the shares or the cash to secure the put, which is the

00:11:52.667 --> 00:11:57.727
difference from naked options. Less leverage, fewer margin calls. Compare the

00:11:57.727 --> 00:12:02.647
annualized yield on the premium with the stock's 2.5% dividend. Depending on

00:12:02.647 --> 00:12:07.547
volatility, that call income can add about 4 to 6% annualized on top of the

00:12:07.547 --> 00:12:13.494
payout. Open your platform, pull the CM chain, note the bid ask and the 30-day at

00:12:13.494 --> 00:12:17.754
the money covered call premium, annualize it, and stack it against that dividend.

